From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tegra: program CS42448 sysclk from the APE machine driver

tegra_codecs_runtime_setup() only forwards the audio master clock to the
codec (snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk) for a hard-coded allowlist of codecs
(rt565x, rt5640, tas2552). The Cirrus cs42xx8 codec on the "cs42448-tdm"
dai-link is never told its MCLK rate, so cs42xx8 keeps the stale
probe-time clk_get_rate("mclk") value. cs42xx8_hw_params() then computes
ratio = sysclk / rate, fails to match the cs42xx8_ratios[] table, and
rejects every stream with:

    cs42xx8 1-0048: unsupported sysclk ratio
    ASoC: error at snd_soc_dai_hw_params on cs42448: -22

The Tegra side already programs aud_mclk correctly (= srate * mclk-fs =
256*Fs = 12.288 MHz @ 48k via tegra_asoc_utils). Forward that requested
rate to the codec, mirroring the existing rt565x-playback handling, so
the ratio resolves to exactly 256 and TDM playback works.

Signed-off-by: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
---
 sound/soc/tegra/tegra_codecs.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/tegra/tegra_codecs.c
+++ b/sound/soc/tegra/tegra_codecs.c
@@ -239,6 +239,16 @@ int tegra_codecs_runtime_setup(struct snd_soc_card *card,
 			}
 		}
 	}

+	rtd = get_pcm_runtime(card, "cs42448-tdm");
+	if (rtd) {
+		err = snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(rtd->dais[rtd->num_cpus], 0,
+					     aud_mclk, SND_SOC_CLOCK_IN);
+		if (err < 0) {
+			dev_err(card->dev, "cs42448 sysclk not set\n");
+			return err;
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(tegra_codecs_runtime_setup);
